course: dictionary
lesson: 6608
title: Noon and the time of day
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Noon is twelve o'clock in the middle of the day. It is also called midday. The clues in a sentence help you find its meaning. «In the UK and Ireland, tradition says April Fool tricks are done before midday; whoever pranks after noon is the fool.» Midday and noon are the same time, and the words before and after show that noon is the dividing line between morning and afternoon.
explain: Noon is also a time on the clock: 12:00. Things are said to happen before noon or after noon. Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «before midday» make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
explain: Noon is when the sun is about as high as it goes in the sky. That is why it is the middle of the day, and why it is a good time to check your meaning in a sentence.
fact: Noon is 12 o'clock in the daytime, also called midday.
fact: Times before noon are in the morning, and times after noon are in the afternoon.
fact: Around noon, shadows are at their shortest, because the sun is about highest in the sky.
fact: The Earth turns 360 degrees in 24 hours, which is 15 degrees an hour, so noon moves around the planet like a spotlight.
fact: Noon is a palindrome: it reads the same forwards and backwards, like mum, dad and level.
exercise: «We eat lunch at noon.» What is noon? | *12 o'clock in the middle of the day | 6 o'clock in the evening | The very start of the morning | Midnight, when it is dark
exercise: «In the UK and Ireland, tradition says April Fool tricks are done before midday; whoever pranks after noon is the fool.» Find and copy one word that means the same as noon. | morning | midnight | pranks | *midday
exercise: «Shadows are shortest around noon, when the sun is about highest in the sky.» What is the sun doing around noon? | *It is about as high as it goes in the sky | It is hidden under the sea | It is rising in the east | It is setting in the west
test: «The shop opens before noon.» Which time is before noon? | 3 o'clock in the afternoon | 8 o'clock at night | Midnight | *9 o'clock in the morning
test: A child says a match starts at 12:30 p.m. What does p.m. tell you? | It is exactly midnight | *It is after noon | It is always a school day | It is before noon
exam: Earth turns 15 degrees each hour, so noon slides around the planet. Why does each place not have noon at the same time? | Because clocks are changed at noon | Because the sun moves around the Earth at night | *Because the Earth turns, so different places reach noon at different times | Because the Earth stops turning at noon
